{%- comment -%}
  A bottle photo trimmed to the bottle itself, so it can stand on a pedestal.

  The store's product photos are all 600x800 with the bottle in the same
  place: about 35%–65% across and 23%–80% down, the rest transparent. Shown
  as they are, the bottle is small and its base floats 20% of the photo above
  whatever sits under it. `.lp-bottle` is a box the size of the bottle; the
  image inside is scaled and shifted so the bottle fills it exactly
  (numbers in lp-blackfriday.css).

  Image overrides set in the theme editor (the campaign renders) are prepared
  on the same 3:4 canvas, so they are trimmed the same way. Pass
  `trimmed: false` to show an image whole instead.

  A photo framed differently can pass its own bottle box as fractions of the
  photo: frame_x, frame_y (top-left corner), frame_w, frame_h. The SiO2 Top
  Sealant photos do this.

  Parameters: image, alt, sizes, widths, width, loading, priority, trimmed,
  frame_x, frame_y, frame_w, frame_h.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign img_width = width | default: 600
  assign img_widths = widths | default: '300,450,600'
  assign img_loading = loading | default: 'lazy'
  assign img_priority = 'auto'
  if priority
    assign img_priority = 'high'
  endif
-%}
{%- if image != blank -%}
  <span
    class="lp-bottle{% if trimmed == false %} lp-bottle--whole{% endif %}"
    {% if frame_w %}style="--bx:{{ frame_x }};--by:{{ frame_y }};--bw:{{ frame_w }};--bh:{{ frame_h }}"{% endif %}
  >
    {{
      image
      | image_url: width: img_width
      | image_tag:
        loading: img_loading,
        fetchpriority: img_priority,
        widths: img_widths,
        sizes: sizes,
        alt: alt
    }}
  </span>
{%- endif -%}
